Project live_indo_react_master {
    database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
    Note: '''
Master reference data: nationwide reaction topics and Indonesian administrative
regions and polling methods. Every topic references a polling method. The cities table includes both kota and kabupaten. Topics are independent
of geography; reactions associate a topic with a location in the reaction database.
No cross-database foreign keys or reaction/heat aggregates are defined here.
seed_history tracks ordered JSON seed versions after schema migrations complete;
its table is created after the PostGIS extension and before the master tables.

Seed files use a version/name/srid/source/records envelope. The numeric version
must match the filename prefix. Each geographic record supplies its master fields,
a GeoJSON MultiPolygon boundary, attribution, and an optional boundary reference
date. Cities supply province_kemendagri_code; the importer resolves province_id
from the existing provinces table rather than assuming generated IDs.
The source object records the pinned upstream revision, raw source SHA-256,
generation metadata, license, and any topology repairs. source.sha256 hashes the
upstream download; seed_history.checksum_sha256 hashes the final local seed file.
An upstream generation timestamp is not a boundary effective date; unknown
boundary_reference_date values remain null. Province seeds are grouped by island:
0001_provinces_sumatera.json through 0007_provinces_papua.json. City/regency seeds
are grouped by province: 0008_cities_aceh.json through
0045_cities_papua_barat_daya.json, ordered by province code. Apply all province
seeds before city/regency seeds. Each file has its own version/history entry;
repaired_region_codes lists only records contained in that file. Version 46 is
0046_polling_methods.json, a locally maintained version/name/records catalog with
agree_disagree, rating, and selection behaviors; it has no geographic metadata.
Apply it after the geographic files. No initial topic catalog is assumed.

Topics reference polling_methods by ID, resolving stable codes rather than assuming
generated IDs. selection_options is an ordered native text array, empty by default.
The master_service validator requires empty options for agree_disagree and rating,
and at least two distinct, nonblank, trimmed labels for selection. Choices are
case-sensitive. Rating responses are integers from 0 through 10; selection
responses choose one option. Application code must preserve method code meanings
and freeze a topic's method/options once responses exist. No business validation
triggers or CHECK constraints are installed here; field validation belongs to
master_service, and response storage/validation is outside this crate.

PostGIS and pg_trgm must be available on the PostgreSQL server. The extension
migration enables both before creating tables and indexes.
This DBML is a design document, not an executable migration.
The DBML CLI may export the custom geometry type as a quoted identifier containing
its parameters. Migrations must use the unquoted SQL type
geometry(MultiPolygon,4326), not "geometry(MultiPolygon,4326)".

Boundaries use 2D geometry(MultiPolygon,4326): WGS84 longitude (X), latitude (Y).
MultiPolygon supports disconnected islands. Normalize imported polygons with
ST_Multi and transform source coordinates with ST_Transform before storage;
ST_SetSRID alone does not reproject coordinates. Use one compatible boundary
source/revision across administrative levels and retain its attribution below.
Migrations do not enforce ST_IsValid or ST_IsEmpty; boundary quality checks are
separate from schema preparation.

Derive map labels with ST_PointOnSurface(boundary), viewport bounds with
ST_Envelope(boundary), and area in square metres with ST_Area(boundary::geography).
Do not treat geometry area in EPSG:4326 as square metres. A label point is not an
administrative capital. Simplify geometry only for map delivery; retain canonical
boundaries here. Validate city/province code and administrative consistency at import;
province_id is the authoritative administrative relationship, not a spatial guess.

DBML's portable index syntax does not express GiST or GIN operator classes.
The SQL migrations define these additional indexes:
CREATE INDEX idx_provinces_boundary_gist ON provinces USING GIST (boundary);
CREATE INDEX idx_cities_boundary_gist ON cities USING GIST (boundary);
CREATE INDEX idx_indonesia_boundary_gist ON indonesia_boundary USING GIST (boundary);
CREATE INDEX idx_topics_name_trgm ON topics USING GIN (name gin_trgm_ops);
CREATE INDEX idx_provinces_name_trgm ON provinces USING GIN (name gin_trgm_ops);
CREATE INDEX idx_cities_name_trgm ON cities USING GIN (name gin_trgm_ops);
These are additional to the B-tree indexes declared below. Trigram indexes support
name search with LIKE/ILIKE and trigram similarity operators. Do not substitute
B-tree indexes for these spatial or trigram indexes when exporting to SQL.

IDs are stable internal references; codes and slugs remain reserved after soft
deletion. Retire regions/topics with is_active or deleted_at rather than removing
historical references. Reads exclude deleted rows; selectable cities also require
an active, nondeleted parent province. Writers set updated_at on actual updates;
its default is intentionally absent. No user/actor tables are assumed.

References:
https://postgis.net/docs/using_postgis_dbmanagement.html
https://postgis.net/docs/ST_PointOnSurface.html
https://dbml.dbdiagram.io/docs/
'''
}


Table seed_history [headercolor: #64748B] {
    Note: 'Append-only record of successfully applied seed files, ordered by numeric filename prefix. MAX(version) gives the last successful version. The seed runner must serialize execution, verify checksums of applied files, and commit each seed and its history row in one transaction. Failed/rolled-back seeds leave no history row; applied files are immutable and corrections require a new version.'

    version         bigint      [pk, not null, note: 'Positive numeric seed filename prefix, e.g. 1 for 0001_provinces_sumatera.json.']
    filename        text        [not null, note: 'Basename only; the runner validates its prefix against version.']
    checksum_sha256 varchar(64) [not null, note: 'Lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 of the exact JSON file bytes.']
    applied_at      timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]

    Indexes {
        filename [unique, name: 'uq_seed_history_filename']
    }
}

Enum city_kind {
    city [note: 'Kota, including administrative cities where applicable.']
    regency [note: 'Kabupaten, including administrative regencies where applicable.']
}

Table polling_methods [headercolor: #8B5CF6] {
    Note: 'Stable polling behaviors, seeded with agree_disagree, rating (0-10), and selection (one choice). Codes remain reserved after soft deletion. Master_service owns code immutability and method-dependent validation.'

    id          bigint      [pk, increment]
    code        text        [not null]
    name        text        [not null]
    description text        [not null, default: '']
    is_active   boolean     [not null, default: true]
    created_at  timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at  timestamptz
    deleted_at  timestamptz

    Indexes {
        code [unique, name: 'uq_polling_methods_code']
        is_active [name: 'idx_polling_methods_is_active']
        deleted_at [name: 'idx_polling_methods_deleted_at']
    }
}

Table topics [headercolor: #F59E0B] {
    Note: 'A nationwide subject people can react to. Disable or soft-delete to close new participation while retaining history. No province/topic join table is required for nationwide availability.'

    id          bigint      [pk, increment]
    slug        text        [not null, note: 'Stable URL/API key; lowercase ASCII words separated by single hyphens.']
    name        text        [not null, note: 'Human-readable topic title.']
    description text        [not null, default: '']
    polling_method_id bigint [not null]
    selection_options text[] [not null, default: `'{}'::text[]`, note: 'Ordered topic choices; empty for nonselection methods by application policy.']
    is_active   boolean     [not null, default: true]
    created_at  timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at  timestamptz
    deleted_at  timestamptz

    Indexes {
        polling_method_id [name: 'idx_topics_polling_method_id']
        deleted_at [name: 'idx_topics_deleted_at']
        is_active [name: 'idx_topics_is_active']
        slug [unique, name: 'uq_topics_slug']
    }
}

Table provinces [headercolor: #059669] {
    Note: 'Indonesian province master data. Store a canonical 2D boundary and keep codes as text; do not hard-code province counts. Topological boundary validity is not enforced by the database. Geographic indexes and derived map values are specified in the project note.'

    id                      bigint      [pk, increment]
    kemendagri_code         varchar(2)  [not null, note: 'Two-digit province code from the selected Kemendagri reference edition; separate from BPS codes.']
    name                    text        [not null, note: 'Official province name.']
    boundary                geometry(MultiPolygon,4326) [not null]
    boundary_source         text        [not null, note: 'Dataset/publisher reference including version or release identifier and attribution.']
    boundary_reference_date date        [note: 'Effective/reference date of the source boundaries, when supplied; not the import timestamp.']
    is_active               boolean     [not null, default: true]
    created_at              timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at              timestamptz
    deleted_at              timestamptz

    Indexes {
        deleted_at [name: 'idx_provinces_deleted_at']
        is_active [name: 'idx_provinces_is_active']
        kemendagri_code [unique, name: 'uq_provinces_kemendagri_code']
    }
}

Table cities [headercolor: #2563EB] {
    Note: 'Second-level administrative regions: cities (kota) and regencies (kabupaten). Every record has exactly one parent province. Names need not be globally unique; kind distinguishes a city from a same-named regency. This table does not represent kecamatan or villages.'

    id                      bigint      [pk, increment]
    province_id             bigint      [not null]
    kemendagri_code         varchar(5)  [not null, note: 'Full province-prefixed Kemendagri code in PP.CC form. Import must verify that PP matches the parent province code.']
    kind                    city_kind   [not null]
    name                    text        [not null, note: 'Official city/regency name; preserve local spelling.']
    boundary                geometry(MultiPolygon,4326) [not null]
    boundary_source         text        [not null, note: 'Dataset/publisher reference including version or release identifier and attribution.']
    boundary_reference_date date        [note: 'Effective/reference date of the source boundaries, when supplied.']
    is_active               boolean     [not null, default: true]
    created_at              timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at              timestamptz
    deleted_at              timestamptz

    Indexes {
        deleted_at [name: 'idx_cities_deleted_at']
        is_active [name: 'idx_cities_is_active']
        kemendagri_code [unique, name: 'uq_cities_kemendagri_code']
        (province_id, kind, name, id) [name: 'idx_cities_province_kind_name', note: 'Parent lookup and ordered city/regency listing; province_id is the leading FK column.']
    }
}

Table indonesia_boundary [headercolor: #DC2626] {
    Note: 'Singleton national boundary for country containment, including Indonesian waters outside province boundaries. Boundary data must cover the intended legal geography; province boundaries are not a substitute. id is constrained to 1 so the table holds one national boundary.'

    id                      smallint    [pk, default: 1]
    boundary                geometry(MultiPolygon,4326) [not null]
    boundary_source         text        [not null, note: 'Dataset/publisher reference including version or release identifier and attribution.']
    boundary_reference_date date        [note: 'Effective/reference date of the source boundary, when supplied.']
    created_at              timestamptz [not null, default: `NOW()`]
    updated_at              timestamptz
}

Ref fk_cities_province: cities.province_id > provinces.id [delete: restrict, update: restrict]

Ref fk_topics_polling_method: topics.polling_method_id > polling_methods.id [delete: restrict, update: restrict]
